# Everything here is optional. Without a key, each feature falls back to
# something that still works and says so in the UI. The server's value always
# wins over anything the browser offers.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, REPLICATE_API_TOKEN and VERCEL_TOKEN can be held in the
# browser instead (the key button in the top bar, ⌘⇧K): the Builder's routes
# take each as a header. The renderer's token is meant to be held there, and
# a value here is only a fallback for it.
# The rest are read by the server alone, so they have to be here or in your
# host's environment. The GitHub mark in the top bar opens `repository` from
# site.config.ts and needs no token.

# The Builder's "Generate" dialog: plan, critique, prompts, finish, ideas,
# ask, build. Without it you copy the blueprint into any agent.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The renderer: a drawn part's body, drawn rather than written. Vector goes to
# recraft-ai/recraft-v3-svg and comes back as SVG; raster goes to
# black-forest-labs/flux-2-pro and comes back as a data: URI. $0.08 and $0.04 a
# call, so it is the one key meant to be the person's own: paste it under the
# key button and it rides with each call. A value here is a silent fallback for
# a deployment that would rather pay centrally. Without either, the body is
# written by Claude instead and the dialog says why.
# REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=

# The tweet console: post to X from the app. See docs/X-KEYS.md.
# Without them, Send opens X's compose page with the words.
X_API_KEY=
X_API_SECRET=
X_ACCESS_TOKEN=
X_ACCESS_SECRET=
# X_HANDLE=yourhandle
# X_MEDIA_API=v2

# Publish: push the site (site/document.json, the blueprint, any generated
# code) to a GitHub repository in one commit. A fine-grained token with
# Contents: read and write on that repository.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
GITHUB_REPO=owner/name
# GITHUB_BRANCH=main
# The Builds page keeps more than one site and each names where it publishes,
# so a request can ask for a repository other than GITHUB_REPO. It can only
# reach what the token can already reach; set this to narrow it further to a
# fixed list, which is what you want on a Builder anyone can open.
# GITHUB_REPOS=owner/one,owner/two

# Go live: the site is built on Vercel from the repository it was pushed to
# and the address comes back. A token from Account Settings › Tokens. Held in
# the browser keys panel instead if you prefer; the server's wins.
# VERCEL_TOKEN=
# Only if the project belongs to a team, or is not the one connected to the
# repository.
# VERCEL_TEAM=team-slug
# VERCEL_PROJECT=project-name

# Older, and still there: a project that is NOT connected to the repository
# has nothing to deploy on a push, so Push calls this hook afterwards. It
# answers with nothing you can open, which is why Go live does not use it.
# VERCEL_DEPLOY_HOOK=https://api.vercel.com/v1/integrations/deploy/…

# Screenshots and tour recordings on the server need a browser. The cut-down
# one (playwright-core + @sparticuz/chromium) is a dependency and needs no
# setting; a full Playwright install is preferred when there is one, because
# it is the only one that can record video. It is looked for in the project,
# at this path, or in the usual global places.
# PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=/opt/node22/lib/node_modules/playwright
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM=/path/to/chromium
# FFMPEG=/path/to/ffmpeg

# How long a Claude route may wait before it answers itself, in milliseconds
# (the generate, body and reshape routes). Unset, the ceiling is the route's
# own maxDuration, except on Vercel, where it is the hobby plan's minute or
# maxDuration, whichever is less: a budget above the real ceiling never gets
# to fire. A plan with more than a minute says so here.
# STUDIO_ANSWER_BUDGET_MS=290000

# Accounts (the Account page, /account). The owner key is a long secret you
# make up (24+ characters); it alone makes and cancels keys. Set it only in
# Vercel's settings, never here. The Blob token is added by Vercel when a
# private Blob store is connected to the project.
# POLIO_OWNER_KEY=STANDIN_your_owner_key
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=STANDIN_set_by_vercel
# Local runs with no store: keep the account in a folder instead (never used on Vercel).
# POLIO_ACCOUNT_DIR=/tmp/polio-account
